        "speaker": "S1",
        "text": "Seaview Hotel, good morning. Can I help you?"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "S2",
        "text": "Hello. I have a booking for this Friday, for three nights, but I need to change it. My name is David Cole."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "S1",
        "text": "One moment, Mr Cole. Yes, I can see it. A double room for three nights, from Friday the ninth."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "S2",
        "text": "That's right. I would like to stay for four nights instead, until Tuesday morning. Is that possible?"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "S1",
        "text": "Let me check. Yes, we have the same room for Monday night as well. It's ninety pounds a night, so the new total is three hundred and sixty pounds."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "S2",
        "text": "That's fine. Can I also have a room with a sea view? My wife loves the sea."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "S1",
        "text": "The sea-view rooms are on the second floor and they cost ten pounds more each night. But they are all booked that weekend, I'm afraid. Only a room facing the garden is available."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "S2",
        "text": "Oh, that's a pity. The garden room is okay, then."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "S1",
        "text": "Great. Breakfast is included, and it is served from seven thirty to ten o'clock in the dining room."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "S2",
        "text": "Wonderful. What time can we check in?"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "S1",
        "text": "Check-in is from two o'clock, but you can leave your bags at reception if you arrive earlier."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "S2",
        "text": "We'll arrive at about noon, so that's useful. Do you have parking?"
      },
      {
        "speaker": "S1",
        "text": "Yes, there's a car park behind the hotel. It costs five pounds a day."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "S2",
        "text": "Perfect. Thank you for your help."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "S1",
        "text": "You're welcome, Mr Cole. We look forward to seeing you."
      }
